# One offline study over an accepted boundary. Only the deterministic secret scanner runs.
name: Study report retains its accepted scope through source change and damaged evidence
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_MODEL=openai-codex:gpt-5.5
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/report_scope.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
paste-file: @ART/alpha-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 RESULT READY | imported-map
nav-mode:
keys: u
require-live-snap: 25 Viewing Scan | accepted-map
keys: Escape
submit: use sast
submit: options sast:scan
submit: set taskMode manual
submit: set tasks secret-scan
submit: scopes
require-live-snap: 25 ACCEPTED SCOPES | accepted-boundary
keys: p
require-live-snap: 25 PLAN A STUDY | study-form
expect: Selected scope
keys: L
require-live-snap: 30 Draft ready | scoped-draft
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/report_scope.py @TMP_TARGET @ART draft
keys: Down Down Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 15 Total calls | calls-editor
type: 9
keys: Enter Down Enter
require-live-snap: 15 Protected review | review-editor
type: 3
keys: Enter Down Down Down
require-live-snap: 15 Next action | next-step
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 REVIEW PLAN & ALLOWANCE | approval-first-page
keys: End
require-live-snap: 15 y approve | approval-last-page
keys: y
require-live-snap: 30 APPROVED STUDY | approved-study
keys: L
require-live-snap: 20 L starts its fixed jobs | jobs-before-launch
keys: L
require-live-snap: 20 dispatcher pid | dispatcher-started
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/report_scope.py @TMP_TARGET @ART finished
keys: Escape
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/report_scope.py @TMP_TARGET @ART attempt-recorded
submit: workbench
require-live-snap: 25 RESULT READY | scan-result
ask: Does the detached study's completed Scan appear as a result to select, without any manual refresh?
nav-mode:
keys: u
require-live-snap: 25 Viewing Review | selected-scan
keys: Escape
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 Scope: study | report-ready
expect: Boundary:
expect: planned discovery file(s)
expect: Proposal coverage: 1 excluded
expect: not completed scanner coverage
ask: Does the study report state the accepted boundary it was planned under, separately from completed scanner coverage?
keys: p
require-live-snap: 20 Boundary rationale | report-provenance
expect: Excluded excluded.py: Explicit labeled fixture exclusion
ask: Do provenance details expose the boundary rationale, scope reference, source tree and operator exclusion without crowding the study facts?
resize: 160x48
keys: Home
live-snap: report-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: report-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: report-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: report-60x20
resize: 40x12
keys: Home
live-snap: report-40x12-top
keys: End
require-live-snap: 15 provenance | report-40x12-tail
ask: At 40x12, can the operator page from the study scope to the complete tail without losing report controls?
resize: 120x36
keys: Home j j j End
require-live-snap: 20 format json (4/6) | json-format
keys: Enter End
require-live-snap: 30 Enter Retry | first-export
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/report_scope.py @TMP_TARGET @ART first
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_MODEL=openai-codex:gpt-5.5 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: report
require-live-snap: 30 Scope: study | report-after-restart
expect: Boundary:
expect: Proposal coverage: 1 excluded
ask: After actual exit and no-color restart, does Report recover the same study and its accepted boundary without starting work?
keys: j j j End
require-live-snap: 20 format json (4/6) | restarted-format
keys: Enter End
require-live-snap: 30 Enter Retry | restarted-export
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/report_scope.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/report_scope.py @TMP_TARGET @ART damage
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | damaged-restart
submit: report
require-live-snap: 30 study receipt unavailable | damaged-report
expect: scope evidence is unavailable
expect: s selects workspace history
keys: j j j End
require-live-snap: 20 format json (4/6) | damaged-format
keys: Enter End
require-live-snap: 15 Press s | refused-export
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/report_scope.py @TMP_TARGET @ART damaged
ask: With the accepted scope evidence missing, is study export blocked with a readable reason and an explicit workspace-history choice, leaving the previous export untouched?
keys: s
require-live-snap: 20 Scope: workspace history | workspace-history
expect: +2 more run(s)
ask: Does workspace history disclose that it makes no study or boundary claim, while naming all three runs of the displayed attempt?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/report_scope.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restore
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/report_scope.py @TMP_TARGET @ART change-source
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | source-changed-restart
submit: report
require-live-snap: 30 Recorded on earlier source | report-after-source-change
expect: Scope: study
expect: Boundary:
expect: phase:Map
ask: After an unrelated source file changed, does Report show the earlier study, clearly labeled as recorded on earlier source, with export available?
keys: j j j End
require-live-snap: 20 format json (4/6) | drift-format
keys: Enter End
require-live-snap: 30 Enter Retry | drift-export
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/report_scope.py @TMP_TARGET @ART drift
keys: Escape
submit: workbench
require-live-snap: 25 Viewing Map | drift-map
keys: BTab
require-live-snap: 25 Secret scan | scan-earlier-source
expect: selected · earlier source
ask: Does the Scan page show the selected three-run attempt as earlier-source history rather than a single legacy run?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
